  <section class="page-intro"><p class="kicker">MEMBER RESOURCE CENTER</p><h1>Small steps. Stronger money habits.</h1><p>Short guides for educators and families. All information is general and for this mockup.</p></section>
  <div class="resource-list"><article id="budgeting"><h2>Plan a school-year budget</h2><p>List take-home income, fixed bills, seasonal costs, and a small savings target. Revisit the plan when the school calendar changes.</p><a href="Loans.aspx#calculator">Try the monthly payment estimator &raquo;</a></article><article id="student-money"><h2>Talk about money with students</h2><p>Use everyday choices to discuss needs, wants, saving, and comparing prices. Keep examples age-appropriate and avoid sharing account details.</p><a href="Accounts.aspx#student">See the Student Starter concept &raquo;</a></article><article id="security"><h2>Recognize suspicious messages</h2><p>Pause before clicking unexpected links. Never share passwords or one-time codes. Contact a real financial institution using a verified phone number or saved website address.</p><a href="Contact.aspx#demo-boundary">How this demo handles your data &raquo;</a></article><article id="privacy"><h2>Privacy in this demo</h2><p>This project uses fictional names and synthetic transactions. It is not connected to a bank, school, vendor, or credit bureau. Do not enter personal data.</p><a href="Contact.aspx#demo-boundary">Read the demo boundary &raquo;</a></article></div>
